    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d489">

                <pb facs="0497" n="491" xml:id="pg491"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851R.01/61½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Admiral William D.
                            Leahy, Chief of Staff to the Commander in
                            Chief of the Army and Navy
                    </hi><anchor n="9" xml:id="d489-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-24">December 24,
                        1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The President desires that I bring the attached despatch to your attention and
                    that I prepare for him a draft reply.</p>
                <p>I shall appreciate receiving, as soon as practicable, your suggestions concerning
                    the reply, as well as any comment you may desire to make on the situation
                    discussed in the Prime Minister’s message.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William D. Leahy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d489-a1.xml" xpointer="d489-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d489-f1" n="9" type="source" xml:id="d489-f1-content">
                <p>Addressed to the Secretary of State and the Chief of Staff of the United States
                    Army (Marshall).</p>
            </note>
